# desktop.packages - Tier 3: a full Wayland desktop session (nested or VNC).
#
# WSL2 exposes NO DRM device - only /dev/dxg, via Direct3D12. There is no
# /dev/dri/cardN and no render node.
#
# Hyprland's backend (Aquamarine) always builds a GBM allocator from a DRM
# node and fails without one, so it cannot start here at all. wlroots falls
# back to a shm allocator that needs no DRM node, so the session we actually
# ship is sway with WLR_RENDERER=pixman.
#
# See docs/12-wayland-on-wsl2.md for the full analysis.
#
# Enable with: make build PROFILE=desktop

# --- compositor (this is the one that works) ---
sway
swayidle
swaylock

# --- Hyprland: installed for inspection/learning only; see the doc above.
#     omarchy-wsl-desktop --compositor hyprland will attempt it and explain
#     why it fails. Kept so Omarchy's own hypr* configs remain readable.
hyprland
hyprland-protocols
xdg-desktop-portal-hyprland

# --- Hyprland companions that work without KMS/hardware ---
hyprpicker
hyprlang
hyprutils
hyprlock
hypridle

# --- on-screen display for volume/brightness keys ---
swayosd

# --- screenshot annotation (pairs with grim/slurp) ---
satty

# --- bar, launcher, notifications, wallpaper ---
waybar
wofi
mako
swaybg

# --- Omarchy's Quickshell-based desktop kit ---
quickshell

# --- screenshot / input synthesis ---
grim
slurp
wtype

# --- XWayland so X11-only apps work inside the nested session ---
xorg-xwayland

# --- seat management (wlroots links against libseat) ---
seatd

# --- remote access for the "desktop in a window" mode ---
wayvnc

# --- polkit agent so GUI privilege prompts resolve ---
polkit-gnome

# --- audio (WSLg provides a PulseAudio server; pipewire clients still help) ---
pipewire
pipewire-pulse
wireplumber
pamixer
